# BixBench bix-13-q5 — DESeq2-style DE relative to JBX1

## Inputs (inspected)
- `data/experiment_metadata.csv`: 36 rows x 5 cols (SampleNumber, AzentaName
  resub-1..36, Media, Strain, Replicate). Strain unique {1,97,98,99}; Media
  {MMGluFeMinus, MMGluFePlus, Succinate}; Replicate {A,B,C}. Fully balanced:
  3 samples per (Media x Strain); 9 per strain; 12 per media.
- `data/raw_counts.csv`: 5828 genes (PA14_*), first (unnamed) column = gene id,
  36 sample columns resub-1..resub-36. Column ORDER IS REVERSED vs metadata;
  mapped by column NAME == metadata AzentaName. No missing, no duplicate genes,
  only 4 single zero counts; no gene is zero in all samples. Per-gene totals
  203 .. 10.5M; per-sample libraries 17.5M .. 28.1M.
- Reference JBX1 = Strain "1" (9 samples).
- Environment: Python 3.12 (numpy/scipy/pandas/statsmodels). No R/Bioconductor,
  no network, no pydeseq2 -> DESeq2 default pipeline re-implemented faithfully.

## Analysis (script: deseq2_final.py; sensitivity: deseq2_strain_only.py)
Design ~ Media + Strain, reference Strain="1". Contrasts: strain 97, 98, 99 vs 1.
- Size factors: median of ratios (5824 genes with all-positive counts), range
  0.767-1.394, mean ~1.0.
- Dispersion: 2 passes (NB-GLM IRLS -> per-gene Cox-Reid APL MLE), then
  parametric quadratic log(log-disp ~ log-baseMean) trend, then empirical-Bayes
  MAP (weighted avg in log space with per-gene variance + floor at trend, the
  DESeq2/pydeseq2 rule; 3449 genes floored to trend).
  gene-wise median 0.0438; trend median 0.0484; MAP median 0.0551.
- LFC: NB-GLM MLE, log link, Var=mu+disp*mu^2. Wald test, t-dist, df=30.
- padj: Benjamini-Hochberg over genes passing independent filtering by baseMean
  (DESeq2 results() default; only 1 gene filtered per strain; count identical
  without independent filtering). NA padj = not significant.
- Cook's distance outlier replacement: cutoff qf(0.99,6,30)=3.47, 0 genes flagged.

## Results (primary)
- DE per strain vs JBX1 (padj<0.05): strain 97 -> 1131; 98 -> 1667; 99 -> 3253.
- Double-mutant candidate (largest footprint -> Delta-lasI Delta-rhlI): strain 99;
  single mutants: strains 97 and 98 (exchangeable: criterion uses their union).
- Final operation:
    count = |{ g : (padj97<0.05 OR padj98<0.05) AND NOT (padj99<0.05) }|
  single-union = 2179; those also significant in double = 1965;
  FINAL = 214 genes.

## Sensitivity / decisions that change the count
- Design ~ Media + Strain (PRIMARY, media as covariate): 214
- Design ~ Strain only (media ignored): 92
- MAP dispersion, no independent filtering: 214
- gene-wise CR dispersion (no MAP shrinkage): 265
- trend-only dispersion: 290
(Under every setting the double-mutant candidate is strain 99.)
